# s83 pre-registration stub, frozen Sun Oct 18 04:20:16 PDT 2026 (clock read with date) after fixture pass 4 PASS (runs/s83/fixture.txt)
# Model: HLT homophonic letter/syllable/chunk-in-core cipher + per-line sticky affix table (core-first back-off), 24 configs
#   plaintext {latin CREMMA, italian dante} x unit {letter, syllable, chunk} x p {0.5, 0.9} x cadence {off, on};
#   per config fitted on training quires: r {0,0.25,0.5}, a {0.75,1.0}, g {0.75,1.25,2.0} (cadence on).
# SELECTION: on each fold SEL = config with the smallest TRAINING fit loss (R(d), types, Moran, pm1, pm3, K100 core order);
#   no held-out quantity enters fitting or selection; the 24 fixed configs are descriptive (multiplicity).
# C1 (primary, s67/s71 rule): SEL PREDICTS held-out quires iff >= 5/6 of P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P7 on >= 8/15 folds on ZL3b, RF1b AND IT2a.
# C2: matched-K (s80 M-freq) core order of SEL within Voynich's band (min..max of training quires) with agreeing permutation-p
#     decision (p<0.05, 200 exact within-line permutations, L-171) at K=50,100,200 on >= 8/15 folds on each transliteration.
# C3: R(1) > 1 and all 7 s69 calls equal the real held-out quire's on >= 8/15 folds on each transliteration.
# READINGS: C1 true -> 'a plaintext-carrying cipher predicts the manuscript out of sample: candidate for a solver run';
#   C1 false, C2 and C3 true -> 'matches the core and slot layers, misses (named predictions)';
#   otherwise -> 'this construction does not reproduce the manuscript' with the failing components named.
